Subject: [PATCH 06883/11362] [outer-loop] ARC bp35+su15 round-5: timed out,
 unverified progress preserved

Both round-5 fable-5 attempts (bp35 L6, su15 L9) timed out (2400s) before
writing artifacts -- nothing verified or banked. Transcript context
preserved for a future attempt:

- bp35: reconfirmed the L4->L5 prefix; found toggling both lower X blocks
  alone is insufficient (gravity flip immediately after is lethal) --
  refines but does not contradict round-4's shield/shaft route.
- su15: deepened the hostile-fusion-chain mechanic (two 7s fuse into e,
  e converts 8 into c, e+e -> d) and diagnosed why the prior line stalled
  (forming f first splits predator targeting); was mid-test on a
  form-d-first reordering when the timeout hit.

No registry count changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
